From a209d3d931d18cac29daad6f3b4ebe65f3d0784f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Yves Le Borgne <pylaterreur@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:26:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make streaming AEAD streams safe to close from their
 finalizers.

io.IOBase.__del__ calls close() on any stream that is not closed yet,
including one whose __init__ raised. Since Python 3.13 it reports
exceptions from that call (gh-62948), and close() raised there in two
cases:

- RewindableInputStream, RawEncryptingStream and
  _DecryptingStreamWrapper raised AttributeError when their __init__
  had failed, e.g. on an unreadable or unwritable file, because close()
  used attributes that were not set yet.
- When closing the wrapped stream failed, close() raised before the
  stream was marked closed, so the finalizer called close() again. For
  RawEncryptingStream, that raised "FAILED_PRECONDITION: Stream closed".

Each one printed "Exception ignored in: ..." on stderr, 10 times in the
streaming AEAD tests on Python 3.13 and 3.14. close() now skips what
__init__ did not set up, and marks the stream closed even if closing
the wrapped stream fails, as io.IOBase.close() does when flush() fails.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GwUvhmzgfkiZ6vo4uGyesN
